    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40861" root="هت" body-key="h">
    
      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَتْهَتَ</span></b>  <i>He urged</i> a camel (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَجَرَهُ</span>) <i>on
the occasion of drinking, by the cry</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَتْ هَتْ</span>.
(AHeyth, K.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَتْ</span>, below. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَتْهَتَ</span>, inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَتْهَتَةٌ</span>; as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَهْتَهَ</span>; <i>He twisted,</i> or <i>distorted, his
tongue in speaking.</i> (Az.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هتهت</span>; (and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَتَّ</span></b> , TA, [aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَتِ3َ</span></b> ?];) <i>He was quick,</i> or <i>rapid,</i>
in his speech. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَتَّ</span>.

